    "evidence": "Strong cyber-editorial identity, disciplined cyan/red semantics, and responsive restructuring of the mandate chain. However, the desktop headline is disproportionately dominant, dense mono labels become extremely small, and the tablet/mobile header feels clipped and crowded. Mobile content is readable but visually compressed, with tight card padding and a miniature intent/outcome graphic. These issues keep it below genuinely polished demo-ready quality.",
